	.asciz	"%ld AI, %ld WEAPONS"

l_.str.1515:                            ; @.str.1515
	.asciz	"Tag Injection"

l_.str.1516:                            ; @.str.1516
	.asciz	"On: a campaign level played alone can be given a profile's weapons and AI, by the randomizer or as a campaign profile says. A screen before the level chooses which, or none.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1517:                            ; @.str.1517
	.asciz	"Campaign Profiles"

l_.str.1518:                            ; @.str.1518
	.asciz	"How a campaign level played alone plays a profile's weapons and AI, in the randomizer's place: the level's weapons and enemies swapped for them, and the weapons its AI hold. The screen before the level chooses one.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1519:                            ; @.str.1519
	.asciz	"Multiplayer Profiles"

l_.str.1520:                            ; @.str.1520
	.asciz	"How a multiplayer game on the game's own maps plays a profile's weapons: swapped for the map's, and as the players' loadouts. Server Setup's TAG PROFILE chooses one for a game you host; its players download the weapons from you.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1521:                            ; @.str.1521
	.asciz	"Tag Profiles"

l_.str.1522:                            ; @.str.1522
	.asciz	"The profiles, each with its tags' size. A lists them, to see a profile's tags, turn them on or off and change their settings.\n \nThere NEW PROFILE makes one. Each is a folder of the tag_injector folder, beside the maps folder."

l_.str.1523:                            ; @.str.1523
	.asciz	"Maps"

l_.str.1524:                            ; @.str.1524
	.asciz	"The Custom Edition maps of custom_maps, singleplayer and multiplayer, by their folders.\n \nA lists them, to add their weapons and AI to a profile."

l_.str.1525:                            ; @.str.1525
	.asciz	"No profiles"

l_.str.1526:                            ; @.str.1526
	.asciz	"NEW PROFILE makes one, to add tags to. Each is a folder of the tag_injector folder, beside the maps folder."

l_.str.1527:                            ; @.str.1527
	.asciz	"A lists its tags: there DUPLICATE PROFILE copies it, and DELETE PROFILE, twice, deletes it"

l_.str.1528:                            ; @.str.1528
	.asciz	"Try out all the weapon and enemy tags from your profile.\n \nWhen holding a weapon, you're able to edit its values (like HUD element positions, name, category, damage, etc) from the overlay menu.\n \nYou'll be able to see all enemies and their animations, as well as spawn them into a small arena to fight them and make sure everything works properly."

l_.str.1529:                            ; @.str.1529
	.asciz	"%ld %s.\n \n%s"

l_.str.1530:                            ; @.str.1530
	.asciz	"A lists them, to turn them on or off and change their settings."

l_.str.1531:                            ; @.str.1531
	.asciz	"None yet: choose a map in MAPS, then these to add here."

l_.str.1532:                            ; @.str.1532
	.asciz	"None: the randomizer cannot play these yet."

l_.str.1533:                            ; @.str.1533
	.asciz	"No %s yet: choose a map in MAPS, then its %s to add here."

l_.str.1534:                            ; @.str.1534
	.asciz	"missing: it is left out"

l_.str.1535:                            ; @.str.1535
	.asciz	"%s%s from %s, %s%s.\n \n%s: the randomizer %s it.\n \nLeft or right turns it %s. A opens its settings%s."

l_.str.1536:                            ; @.str.1536
	.asciz	", replacing the original"

l_.str.1537:                            ; @.str.1537
	.asciz	"plays"

l_.str.1538:                            ; @.str.1538
	.asciz	"leaves out"

l_.str.1539:                            ; @.str.1539
	.asciz	": its name, faction, class, custom type and HUD"

l_.str.1540:                            ; @.str.1540
	.asciz	": its name, faction, type and custom type"

l_.str.1541:                            ; @.str.1541
	.asciz	": its name"

l_.str.1542:                            ; @.str.1542
	.asciz	"The name the menus show it by: %s.\n%s %s\n \nA types another. Nothing typed is the last part of its path. Its path stays its map's: a level knows it by it."

l_.str.1543:                            ; @.str.1543
	.asciz	"%sOn: the randomizer plays it. Off: it stays in the profile, and is left out.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1544:                            ; @.str.1544
	.asciz	"The weapon pools it joins: COVENANT's or HUMAN's.\n \nAUTO: by its name (a plasma, needle or carbine weapon is the Covenant's).\n \nLeft and right choose another."

l_.str.1545:                            ; @.str.1545
	.asciz	"The enemy pool it joins: COVENANT, FLOOD or HUMAN, or ANY's alone.\n \nAUTO: by its unit's name (a grunt, elite, jackal, hunter or engineer is the Covenant's, a flood form the Flood's, a marine human). A brute is none of them: choose COVENANT.\n \nLeft and right choose another."

l_.str.1546:                            ; @.str.1546
	.asciz	"The campaign's type it counts as for ONE TYPE: as an ELITE, it is among the elites a pool of one type plays.\n \nAUTO: by its unit's name. NONE: no type's.\n \nLeft and right choose another."

l_.str.1547:                            ; @.str.1547
	.asciz	"The weapon pool it joins: PRECISION, AUTOMATIC or POWER.\n \nAUTO: by its name (a sniper or a pistol is precision, a rocket or a shotgun power, a rifle automatic). NONE: none of them.\n \nLeft and right choose another."

l_.str.1548:                            ; @.str.1548
	.asciz	"The randomizer's ONE TYPE has TAG INJECTOR, and its CUSTOM TYPE these: the profile's %s of the custom type %s alone. Give tags the same one (BRUTE) to play them together.\n \nA types it. Nothing typed is its name."

l_.str.1549:                            ; @.str.1549
	.asciz	"AI"

l_.str.1550:                            ; @.str.1550
	.asciz	"The HUD it is drawn with, whoever carries it (an AI of the profile too). OWN: its map's. STOCK: the campaign's HUD of the weapon chosen (its zoom and ammo art; the weapon zooms and fires as it did). AUTO: by its name, else by its zoom and magazine.\n \nLeft and right choose another."

l_.str.1551:                            ; @.str.1551
	.asciz	"ON: it takes the place of the campaign's tag of its path, with the tags it names as its map has them, wherever the level has that tag (its own, or one the randomizer copies).\n \nOFF: the level's stays, and this one joins the pools as it is.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1552:                            ; @.str.1552
	.asciz	"A, twice, takes it out of %s and deletes its bundle. Its map can add it again.\n \nTo leave it out for now, turn it off."

l_.str.1553:                            ; @.str.1553
	.asciz	"Add To"

l_.str.1554:                            ; @.str.1554
	.asciz	"No profiles: NEW PROFILE makes one, to add tags to."

l_.str.1555:                            ; @.str.1555
	.asciz	"The profile a map's tags are added to: %s. Left and right choose another.\n \nVIEW PROFILE, here and in the maps' lists, shows it."

l_.str.1556:                            ; @.str.1556
	.asciz	"Custom Singleplayer"

l_.str.1557:                            ; @.str.1557
	.asciz	"Custom Multiplayer"

l_.str.1558:                            ; @.str.1558
	.asciz	"%d Custom Edition %s maps.\n \nA lists their folders of custom_maps, and the maps beside them."

l_.str.1559:                            ; @.str.1559
	.asciz	"campaign"

l_.str.1560:                            ; @.str.1560
	.asciz	"multiplayer"

l_.str.1561:                            ; @.str.1561
	.asciz	"No maps"

l_.str.1562:                            ; @.str.1562
	.asciz	"No Custom Edition maps of this kind: put them in custom_maps."

l_.str.1563:                            ; @.str.1563
	.asciz	"A folder of custom_maps: %d maps.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1564:                            ; @.str.1564
	.asciz	"A %s map%s%s.\n \nA lists its weapons, AI and the rest, to add to %s."

l_.str.1565:                            ; @.str.1565
	.asciz	", in "

l_.str.1566:                            ; @.str.1566
	.asciz	"a profile"

l_.str.1567:                            ; @.str.1567
	.asciz	"No multiplayer profiles"

l_.str.1568:                            ; @.str.1568
	.asciz	"NEW PROFILE makes one, playing the weapons of a profile of TAG PROFILES. Each is a file of the tag_injector folder's multiplayer folder."

l_.str.1569:                            ; @.str.1569
	.asciz	"Its profile (%s) is not there: A, then TAG PROFILE, chooses another."

l_.str.1570:                            ; @.str.1570
	.asciz	"Plays the %ld weapons on of %s.\n \nA opens its settings: there DELETE PROFILE, twice, deletes it."

l_.str.1571:                            ; @.str.1571
	.asciz	"The name the menus and Server Setup show it by.\n \nA types another."

l_.str.1572:                            ; @.str.1572
	.asciz	"The profile whose weapons on it plays (%ld of them): its weapons alone, not its AI or equipment. A game you host shares them with its players, who download them from you.\n \nA, left and right choose another."

l_.str.1573:                            ; @.str.1573
	.asciz	"ADD TO MAP'S: the profile's weapons join the map's, so a weapon may be either. PROFILE'S ONLY: the map's weapons are all the profile's.\n \nWith MANUAL, ADD keeps the map's weapon among those chosen for it.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1574:                            ; @.str.1574
	.asciz	"How the map's weapons are swapped:\nFULLY RANDOM: any weapon, each time one spawns.\nONCE PER POSITION: each place rolls once a game.\nONCE PER WEAPON: each of the map's weapons rolls once (every shotgun the same).\nMANUAL: the weapons chosen for each.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1575:                            ; @.str.1575
	.asciz	"The weapons that take the place of the map's %s, one at random each time it spawns. None chosen: it stays as it is.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1576:                            ; @.str.1576
	.asciz	"The weapons each player spawns with.\nGAMETYPE'S: as the gametype gives them.\nRANDOM: two of the weapons a map's weapon may be swapped for.\nSET: the two chosen below.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1577:                            ; @.str.1577
	.asciz	"A weapon each player spawns with: one of the profile's, or one of the map's (when the map has it).\n \nA, left and right choose another."

l_.str.1578:                            ; @.str.1578
	.asciz	"No campaign profiles"

l_.str.1579:                            ; @.str.1579
	.asciz	"NEW PROFILE makes one, playing the weapons and AI of a profile of TAG PROFILES. Each is a file of the tag_injector folder's campaign folder."

l_.str.1580:                            ; @.str.1580
	.asciz	"Plays the %ld weapons and %ld AI on of %s.\n \nA opens its settings: there DELETE PROFILE, twice, deletes it."

l_.str.1581:                            ; @.str.1581
	.asciz	"The name the menus show it by.\n \nA types another."

l_.str.1582:                            ; @.str.1582
	.asciz	"The profile whose weapons (%ld) and AI (%ld) on it plays.\n \nA, left and right choose another."

l_.str.1583:                            ; @.str.1583
	.asciz	"How the weapons lying in the level are swapped for the profile's.\n \nA opens them."

l_.str.1584:                            ; @.str.1584
	.asciz	"How the level's enemies are swapped for the profile's AI, and the weapons each kind and rank of them holds (its LOADOUT).\n \nA opens them."

l_.str.1585:                            ; @.str.1585
	.asciz	"Enemies"

l_.str.1586:                            ; @.str.1586
	.asciz	"Weapons"

l_.str.1587:                            ; @.str.1587
	.asciz	"ADD TO LEVEL'S: the profile's %s join the level's, so one may stay as it is. PROFILE'S ONLY: they are all the profile's.\n \nWith MANUAL, ADD keeps the level's own among those chosen for it.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1588:                            ; @.str.1588
	.asciz	"How the level's enemies are swapped:\nRANDOM: any of the profile's AI, each placed (your allies stay as they are).\nMANUAL: the AI chosen for each enemy (and rank) below.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1589:                            ; @.str.1589
	.asciz	"How the level's weapons, lying in it or held by its AI, are swapped:\nRANDOM: any of the profile's weapons, each placed.\nMANUAL: the weapons chosen for each of the campaign's.\n \nLeft and right choose."

l_.str.1590:                            ; @.str.1590
	.asciz	"The weapons that take the place of the level's %s, lying in it or held by its AI (who keep it when they cannot hold them), one at random each placed. None chosen: it stays as it is.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1591:                            ; @.str.1591
	.asciz	"The level's %ss, each rank its own: the AI that take its place, and the weapons it holds.\n \nA lists its ranks."

l_.str.1592:                            ; @.str.1592
	.asciz	"The AI that take the place of the level's %ss%s.\n \nA opens them."

l_.str.1593:                            ; @.str.1593
	.asciz	", and the weapons it holds"

l_.str.1594:                            ; @.str.1594
	.asciz	"On: %s may take the place of the level's %s, one of those on at random each placed.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1595:                            ; @.str.1595
	.asciz	"the level's own"

l_.str.1596:                            ; @.str.1596
	.asciz	", and the weapons they hold"

l_.str.1597:                            ; @.str.1597
	.asciz	"The AI that take its place, one of those on at random each placed. None chosen: it stays as it is.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1598:                            ; @.str.1598
	.asciz	"ENEMIES' REPLACEMENT is RANDOM: any of the profile's AI takes its place. MANUAL chooses them here."

l_.str.1599:                            ; @.str.1599
	.asciz	"The weapons it holds (it, or the AI that took its place), one of those on that it can hold, at random. None chosen: its own, swapped as WEAPONS says.\n \nA lists them."

l_.str.1600:                            ; @.str.1600
	.asciz	"On: it may hold %s%s.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1601:                            ; @.str.1601
	.asciz	"its own weapon"

l_.str.1602:                            ; @.str.1602
	.asciz	" (when the level has it)"

l_.str.1603:                            ; @.str.1603
	.asciz	"On: %s may take the place of the map's %s, one of those on at random each time it spawns.\n \nA, left or right turns it on or off."

l_.str.1604:                            ; @.str.1604
	.asciz	"the map's own"

l_.str.1605:                            ; @.str.1605
	.asciz	"None here."

l_.str.1606:                            ; @.str.1606
	.asciz	"A lists them, to add to the profile."

l_.str.1607:                            ; @.str.1607
	.asciz	"A lists them. The randomizer cannot play these yet."

l_.str.1608:                            ; @.str.1608
	.asciz	"%ld tags required. The randomizer cannot play these yet."

l_.str.1609:                            ; @.str.1609
